# Local Security Reviewer

Use the local Ollama + SQLite RAG agent (not Cursor Cloud) to detect security concerns:

```bash
./scripts/pr-review-index.sh   # shared RAG index (with PR reviewer)
./scripts/sec-review.sh        # current branch
./scripts/sec-review.sh --pr 42
```

Rules: `agents/security-reviewer/RULES.md`.
Index: `agents/pr-reviewer/index/rag.sqlite` (shared).

Focus on:

- Hardcoded secrets / API keys / tokens in source
- Cleartext `http://` endpoints and TLS/certificate bypasses
- Insecure storage (`SharedPreferences` for secrets)
- Sensitive logging (`print` / `debugPrint` of tokens/PII)
- Risky WebView settings and unvalidated URL / deep-link launches
- Debug auth/security bypasses that can ship

Keep findings actionable and file-scoped. Prefer evidence from the diff, nearby hunks, prechecks, and RAG — not generic security advice. Never auto-patch or merge.
